Breaking data model changes scores: del:1 + add:0, change matches:
-    _inherit = 'res.users.settings'

Total Changes: 237

[REF] mail, *: read the settings off their record

Before this commit, the settings of a user were a single Settings
record mixing two unrelated things: the res.users.settings row of the
server and the local preferences of the device (sound, push to talk,
blur).

That record has the problem that nothing tells a reader which of its
fields is which, and that the whole server row reaches the store,
columns of modules taking no part in it included (calendar, google,
microsoft, web_enterprise).

This commit turns res.users.settings into a record of its own, reached
from its owner, store.self_user.res_users_settings_id, and sent with
the user through _store_settings_fields, the field list each module
extends with its own columns. A write is broadcast as a plain store
insert built from that same list, so those foreign columns never reach
the store and the dedicated bus channel of the settings is gone.

This commit also turns the volumes of the other users into records of
res.users.settings.volumes, reached from the settings record. The
local preferences stay a singleton, store.settings, holding no server
column, so the livechat dummy settings record at startup is gone.

closes odoo/odoo#279128

Related: odoo/enterprise#126029
Signed-off-by: Sébastien Theys (seb) <seb@odoo.com>

